    <briefdescription>
<para>C++20 concept satisfied when <computeroutput>T</computeroutput> is a valid operand of the approximate comparator. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>The type to be checked, possibly a reference.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
The <computeroutput>approx_operand</computeroutput> concept is satisfied when <computeroutput>T</computeroutput>, or the value it wraps (for the framework value wrappers and the numeric literals), is an arithmetic type other than <computeroutput>bool</computeroutput> and the character types (<computeroutput>char</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>wchar_t</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>char8_t</computeroutput>, <computeroutput>char16_t</computeroutput>, and <computeroutput>char32_t</computeroutput>), which are not numbers; <computeroutput>signed char</computeroutput> and <computeroutput>unsigned char</computeroutput> are accepted, as the integer types they are. </para>
